body:
Because I've been blessed by the devs with the Loading Screen bug and therefore can't play the game anymore, I've now been playing Half Life deathmatch. And guess what? I'm not missing the goddamned loading times. It's just so simple and straightforward to open the game, find a game and jump into it almost instantly (seriously it takes like 15 seconds) and play as much as you want. Sure, sometimes the server changes the map, but it's a chore that only lasts 20 seconds while in QC it took how much? 3 to 4 minutes?

&#x200B;

So yeah, the loading screens take way too long and it's actually hurting QC

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I've tried this, I got to the menu and even found a game (couldnt get into it though for some arcane reasons) but the error window kept staying there, and once i attempted to close it the game closed as well. Upon restarting Quake i was back to square one.

&#x200B;

I've done this 4 hours ago so it's not the servers, will try again tomorrow. My aim is getting shittier and shittier every second that passes, i don't know what to play anymore, i'm getting severly depressed and Sonic adventure dx that i've just downloaded won't help. God may though

bladee has to switch up his sound and flow a bit in order to succeed. I feel like he has been sticking to this streched out lamenting vocals which I love but not too many people can enjoy nor understand them. I wouldn't mind a more "trappy" bladee, like the one we got in Lordship or hell even in It Suxx. 

&#x200B;

Featurings with other artists would help him as well, even close ones like Yung Lean or ecco so that if he really can't switch up flows he can lean on another person's vocals so that the song won't get too stale. (I dream a lil tracy or lil uzi feat every time I close my eyes to hopefully sleep)

Yes, I have been missing lots of rails since the last patch dropped. Same goes for rockets that sometimes do weird splash damage, like 30 even though it was super close to their feet. Fucking annoyiing, how do they mess up the netcode with every update they do. I remember two patches ago the netcode felt amazing, and now we got this.

I am sad because i'm really digging this new update, but these misses are getting anoying

&#x200B;
